  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency support to Rohingya refugees affected by the March 2023 fire in a refugee camp</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to strengthen the protection of Rohingya refugee women, girls, men, and boys in camp 11 through the provision of integrated and lifesaving GBV-SRH and skill development interventions. The IOM project establishes, rehabilitates, and supports 1 integrated Women and Child Friendly Space, benefitting 6,300 women and girls, and sets up 1 Multi-Purpose Centre which will be accessed by 1,000 men and boys. In total, the project provides life-saving assistance to 7,300 people, including 4,500 women, 500 men, 1,800 girls, 500 boys, and 73 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
